{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1790960930,"nonce":"sPu+N31c6tqXmM12MVjH9GOi6ds=","title":"Python: a module body an embedder runs exits the host process on an uncaught exception","message":"A Python module body run through the entry (`__main__`) ends an uncaught exception in zb_uncaught, which prints the traceback and calls zb_exit(1): libc exit from inside the host's call. Importing a Python module that raises therefore kills the host instead of failing the import.\n\nGive embedders a module-body entry that leaves an uncaught exception pending (in the error-flag global) and returns, for example a second declared entry or a zyntax_python option that lowers the body without the zb_uncaught tail. zypy keeps the report-and-exit tail. Related: ffa18fc57b07e80c26e7c4102a0d8443de3aa7f1a539c47d947ed14e91257259 (__name__ of a module an embedder loads). Reported by caribou.","files":null}]}